    {
      "id": "canvas-smoke-notes",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Smoke Test Criteria",
      "root": false,
      "position": {"x": 980, "y": 160},
      "width": 560,
      "height": 520,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "ports": [
        {"id": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "bidirectional", "dataType": "any", "angle": 210}
      ],
      "data": {
        "identity": {"graphId": "canvas-smoke-test"},
        "markdown": "# Canvas Smoke Test\n\n## Native path\n\n- **Wave** renders a visible canvas waveform.\n- **Bars** renders visible canvas bars.\n- Zooming does not leave either panel blank.\n\n## View → Port path\n\n- **Canvas View Source** exposes its canvas at the named payload path `node.web.detail`.\n- Its render shape declares `kind: canvas` with `sourcePath: node.web.detail`.\n- **Canvas View Port** consumes `node.web.detail` from that source node.\n- Pass if the port reproduces the canvas surface instead of showing `MISSING_VIEW`, `No target`, or a blank panel.\n\n## Known issue under investigation\n\nA standalone `port` with its own `data.canvas` currently enters target-resolution behavior instead of rendering the inline canvas payload. This fixture tests the current two-node workaround.\n\nAnimation is intentionally out of scope."
      }
    }
